   "n": 4,
   "image": "books/G1/097/p04.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 856,
   "text": "\"Come on, Hugs,\" Meg said. \"It's time for your dinner.\" She gave Hugs some cat food. Hugs sniffed at the food. Then he turned his head away. \"You don't want that food, do you, Hugs?\" Meg said. \"Do you want chicken today?\" Meg gave Hugs a new can of cat food. But he still did not eat.",
   "textBox": null,
   "wordBoxes": null,
   "audio": [
    0.83,
    15.6
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "image": "books/G1/097/p05.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 856,
   "text": "\"Hugs won't eat!\" Meg said to Gram. \"He won't eat the chicken or beef. He doesn't want the turkey or the turkey with cheese. He won't even eat the tuna!\" \"I can see that,\" said Gram. \"But Hugs loves t o eat,\" said Meg. He never leaves a bit of food in his dish.\" \"He must feel sick,\" said Gram. \"Oh, no! Poor Hugs!\" said Meg. Will he be okay?\"",
   "textBox": null,
   "wordBoxes": null,
   "audio": [
    17.62,
    42.92
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "image": "books/G1/097/p06.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 856,
   "text": "\"Let's call Dr. Jan, the vet,\" said Gram. \"She will know what to do.\" Gram went to call the vet. Meg went with Gram. Then they came back t o the kitchen to get Hugs a nd take him to the vet. But Hugs was gone.",
   "textBox": null,
   "wordBoxes": null,
   "audio": [
    44.3,
    64.7
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "image": "books/G1/097/p07.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 856,
   "text": "\"Gramps, have you seen Hugs?\" M eg asked. \"Let me think,\" said Gramps. \"I read the paper, and he sat on my lap. Then I took the meatballs out of the freezer to thaw, and he watched me. But I haven't seen him since then.\" \"Hugs! Come here, Hugs!\" Meg called. But Hugs did not come to her. \"I'll look in the closets,\" s aid Gram.",
   "textBox": null,
   "wordBoxes": null,
   "audio": [
    65.97,
    80.94
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "image": "books/G1/097/p08.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 856,
   "text": "\"I'll look under the beds,\" s aid Meg. \"I'll help you look,\" said Gramps. T hey looked under all the tables and behind all the curtains. They even looked in the basement. But they didn't find Hugs.",
   "textBox": null,
   "wordBoxes": null,
   "audio": [
    81.98,
    107.21
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "image": "books/G1/097/p09.jpg",
   "w": 1400,
   "h": 856,
   "text": "\"Where is that cat?\" said Meg. \"I just don't know,\" said Gram. \"Maybe he knows you called Dr. Jan,\" said Gramps. \"He doesn't like to go to the vet. He may hide from us for hours!\" Gramps went to put the meatballs in the oven. Meg wanted to look around the house one more time. Soon Meg called, \"Gram! Gramps! I found him! I found Hugs!\" Then Gramps called out, \"I found something, too!\"",
